  "text": "BRISK is a binary descriptor that calculate the weighted Gaussian average over selected points near the keypoint  . For specific pairs of Gaussian windows BRISK compare values that could be either a 1 or a 0 depending on which window in pair was greater  . BRISK descriptor applies the sampling pattern around the keypoints  . The sampling pattern rotated \u03b1 angle around the keypoint k. The \u03b1 is calculated by  :",
